' Lab 3 · Task 3 · Scenario 1 — Classic Registration & Login
' Unified human actor "User"; context role shown via note.
' Consistent with lab3/spec.md, lab1 ERD (+isAuthor), ADR-0007.
' Password hashing/verification: Argon2id.
' Token storage: accessToken in JS memory; refreshToken in HttpOnly cookie.

@startuml
title SchemaPostol - Scenario 1: Classic Registration & Login (01-auth)

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

' ---------- Unified human actor + system + DB entities ----------
actor "User" as HumanUser
participant "Frontend" as FE
participant "Backend" as BE
database "User" as UserEntity
database "Session" as SessionEntity

note right of HumanUser
  Unified actor **User**.
  Context role in this scenario:
  **Guest** before authenticating, becomes a
  **Registered User** after a successful login.
end note

'
' ================= REGISTRATION (UC-01) =================
'
== Registration ==

HumanUser -> FE : click "Register" and enter\nregistration data (nickname, email, password)
activate FE
FE -> BE : POST /auth/register\n{nickname, email, password}
activate BE
BE -> UserEntity : findByEmail(email), findByNickname(nickname)
activate UserEntity
UserEntity --> BE : existing user | null
deactivate UserEntity
alt invalid input - user already exists
  BE --> FE : 409 Conflict {error: "nickname or email already taken"}
else valid input - new user
  BE -> BE : hashPassword(password) using Argon2id
  BE -> UserEntity : INSERT {user_id, nickname, email,\npassword_hash, isAuthor=false, created_at}
  activate UserEntity
  UserEntity --> BE : OK
  deactivate UserEntity
  BE --> FE : 201 Created {userId}
end
deactivate BE
deactivate FE
note over BE : Validation failed -> registration rejected;\notherwise the new User row is persisted.\nFlow continues into the Login scenario (step 2).

'
' ================= LOGIN (UC-02) =================
'
== Login ==

HumanUser -> FE : click "Login" and enter credentials\n(email, password)
activate FE
FE -> BE : POST /auth/login {email, password}
activate BE
BE -> UserEntity : findByEmail(email)
activate UserEntity
UserEntity --> BE : user {user_id, password_hash, isAuthor} | null
deactivate UserEntity
alt no user with such email
  BE --> FE : 401 Unauthorized {error: "invalid credentials"}
else user found
  BE -> BE : verify password via Argon2id(password,\npassword_hash)
  alt password mismatch
    BE --> FE : 401 Unauthorized {error: "invalid credentials"}
  else password matches
    BE -> BE : generate refreshToken (7 days) +\naccessToken (15 min JWT)
    BE -> SessionEntity : createSession(user_id, hash(refreshToken),\nsession info: ip, user_agent)
    activate SessionEntity
    SessionEntity --> BE : session_id
    deactivate SessionEntity
    BE --> FE : 200 OK - accessToken (json) +\nrefreshToken (HttpOnly, Secure, Domain cookie)
  end
end
deactivate BE
note over FE
  **Token storage:** JS stores `accessToken` in memory;
  the browser automatically attaches the `refreshToken`
  HttpOnly cookie on subsequent requests.
end note
deactivate FE

@enduml